<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00016373> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00016373> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2979-8613"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-11-16"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Fatty acid beta-oxidation via glucagon-AMPK-ACACB (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Curated with GO AI HUB. Human glucagon-GCGR-cAMP/PKA and AMPK signalling to CPT1A-dependent mitochondrial fatty acid beta-oxidation, transferred by ISS from mouse gomodel:6ab067da00013223 with human experimental evidence where available."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Human model built 2026-11-16 by ISS transfer from mouse gomodel:6ab067da00013223 (same structure, 12 activities). Mouse experimental evidence -> ISS (ECO:0000250, GO_REF:0000024) with the mouse MGI id(s) of the source gene(s); AMPK complex (GO:0031588) with Prkaa1 MGI:MGI:2145955 | Prkaa2 MGI:MGI:1336173. Rat ISS (RGD) and IC lines kept unchanged. Mouse ISS lines from human proteins replaced by human experimental references: GCG/GCGR/GNAS IDA PMID:32193322 (Qiao 2020); GCGR plasma membrane IDA PMID:9287038 (Buggy 1997); GNAS has input ADCY6 and GNAS -> ADCY6 IDA PMID:17110384 (Gao 2007); PRKACA nucleus IDA PMID:21085490; AMPK cytoplasm IDA GO_REF:0000052 (HPA, PRKAA1 cytosol); CPT2 enabled by IDA PMID:20538056 (Violante 2010); PPARA has input CPT1A and PPARA -> CPT1A IDA PMID:16271724 (Napal 2005; abstract only, full text not checked). Open: CPT2 has output palmitoyl-CoA has no evidence (Violante 2010 assayed the reverse reaction; no human forward-reaction paper found). Full evidence rationale: comments of gomodel:6ab067da00013223."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

